  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of Ghana completed the actuarial valuation of the Social Security and National Insurance Trust (SSNIT) and the report was adopted by the Board of SSNIT in November 2020. The valuation was carried out after consultations with relevant stakeholders including the Ministry of Employment and Labour Relations and the social partners. 
In February 2021, a Social Security Inquiry exercise was completed and contributed to further debate and actions on Social protection classification within the government budget, social protection data management and the budget Monitoring and Evaluation Framework.

The National Health Insurance Scheme implemented a digital platform to facilitate registration and premium collection, in September 2020
 The ILO supported the actuarial valuation for the pension scheme under The Social Security and National Insurance Trust (SSNIT) in 2020, in particular the data collection and analysis, long-term projections, the development of the report and the workshop for the validation.
In addition, the ILO facilitated a training on social protection data collection and monitoring, and supported the data collection and validation for the Social Security Inquiry exercise, in February 2020. The training brought together 40 participants including 14 women coming from the Ministries in charge of finance and social protection, social protection institutions and programmes, the National Statistics Institution and social partners.
ILO provide technical support to SSNIT for the development of the digital platform for registration and premium collection in 2020. A consultant was engaged for the development of the Platform and training of the staff of SSNIT on the use of the digital platform</narrative>
   </description>
